---
#1759: a context declaring a function with the context's own name. The
emitted suite imported the target as a namespace named after it
(`import * as greet`) and destructured `{ greet }` from it inside the case,
reading `greet` in its own temporal dead zone: `tsc` rejected it, and at
runtime it would be a `ReferenceError`. A test module's namespaces now carry a
reserved prefix (`__ns_greet`).
---
context greet

fn greet(name: String) -> String {
  "Hello, \(name)!"
}
